# Secrets and operator-local config. Only .env.example is committed.
.env

# The blocklist is data, not source. Committing an explicit slur and
# illegal-content pattern list would turn this repo into a searchable copy of
# one, and would make every addition a rebuild plus a public diff instead of
# an edit the operator can make during an incident. Only the example is
# committed; see SPEC.md's safety section.
blocklist.txt

# The corpus. bbolt keeps everything in one file, it reaches hundreds of MB
# within weeks, and it holds learned user content, so it is neither
# committable nor something anyone should be able to fetch from the repo.
# Production starts empty on a named volume; see docker-compose.prod.yml.
markov.db
markov.db.lock
*.db.tmp
backups/

# The transcription assets. Nothing in the repository reads these as of M12, which
# shipped the plugin as an Engine seam with no implementation behind it, but the
# entries stay: the reason they were needed has not changed and whoever writes an
# engine will put the files back. ggml-small.bin is 465 MiB, well over GitHub's
# hard 100 MiB per-file limit, so a commit containing it cannot be pushed at all
# and the only remedy is rewriting history. ffmpeg.exe is another 96 MiB.
voicenotes/

# Build output
/bin/
/dist/
/peregrine
/peregrine.exe

*.log
AI_CODE_REVIEW.md
